"use strict";

/* generated from story/scenes/act2_ch10.md — do not edit */

SC["c4_open"]={t:()=>SYS(`CHAPTER TEN — LANTERN RITE`)+P(`Spring arrives the way the basement predicted it would, to the day. The Lantern Rite is the sect's oldest observance: at dusk the whole mountain climbs the thousand steps carrying lights, and at the rite's head the season's honors are read into the rolls — new disciples, new ranks, new names.`)+P(`Yours is read second. <i>The gold-haired servant, received into the outer court with tournament honors.</i> Ten thousand people hear the steward's office choke on every word of it. Somewhere below, the servant terraces make their sound again, and you stand in new robes that smell of cedar and someone else's incense, and let the mountain look at you, because being seen stopped being optional a season ago.`)+((G.f.a2_mei_bench=="star")?(P(`The bench decision is read third. <i>Mei of Cloudrest, apprenticed to the inner court's hall of medicine.</i> She receives it the way she watches kitchen doors — hungry, exact, giving nothing away — and only you, watching her hands, see the fold finally loosen. An outer-court herb girl with no hall and no patron just walked through the one door in the valley, and she did it carrying your secret balanced on her head like a water-jar.`)):(""))+((G.f.a2_mei_bench=="suspect")?(P(`The bench decision is read third. <i>Mei of Cloudrest, apprenticed to the inner court's hall of medicine.</i> The gallery cheers; the clerk behind the judges' table does not, and his small note rides up the mountain with the honors like a burr in a saddle-blanket. She won. The asking isn't over. You both wear it the same way: smiling, balanced, careful as full jars.`)):(""))+((G.f.a2_mei_bench=="robbed")?(P(`The bench decision is read third, and it is the rites-office boy — the sanded-down salve, the borrowed idea, promising. Mei stands in the crowd with her hands folded while a third cousin to somebody collects her future, and you stand in new robes that suddenly weigh what they actually cost. “Sensible,” says the back of her head, without turning around.`)):(""))+P(`And then, last, in a voice that needs no herald's bell: Elder Kang, rising from the elders' terrace to announce that the sect's hospitality will receive its remarkable new disciple <i>personally</i>, tonight, after the lanterns crest the peak. The crowd hears an honor. You hear a door closing, and recognize the latch.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`One day, then. The rite gives you one day, and the mountain seems to know it.`,go:"a2c10_gifts"}]};

SC["a2c10_gifts"]={t:()=>P(`The day arranges itself around you like a held breath, and the people in it come one at a time, each with something that is not quite a goodbye.`)+((G.mei>=3)?(P(`Mei finds you first, in the drying shed where the whole story started, and puts a tiny porcelain vial in your hand. Cloudpith Elixir — a master-work, the kind infirmaries lock up. “If you fall down,” she says, in the voice she uses for dosage instructions, “it picks you back up. ONCE. Don't you dare waste it on dying twice.” ${G.f.a2_mei_bench=="star"?"It is the first thing she has brewed under her new rank, and she spent it on you before the ink on the apprenticeship dried.":G.f.a2_mei_bench=="suspect"?"She brewed it in one night, on borrowed bench-rights, daring the clerk's note to say something.":"She brewed it anyway, hall or no hall, on a borrowed brazier in her grandmother's shed, and it is better than anything the rites-office boy will make in his life."}`)):(""))+((G.f.a2_ring=="cold")?(P(`Bao does not come. A laundry runner finds you at noon instead, with a betting slip folded into quarters: everything he has, on you, at the worst odds the ring would write — <i>servant survives the sect's hospitality.</i> No note. No name. Just the slip, which from Bao is a whole letter, and most of an apology, and not quite a hand extended. He knows exactly what he's betting on tonight. So do you.`)):(P(`Bao walks you up the first hundred steps of the procession route at noon, doing crowd-color like a commentator — who's climbing badly, whose lantern is rented, which elder dyes his beard — until the laughing stops working and he runs dry mid-step. “Firewood boys know everything,” he says finally, to the steps. “So I know where you're being received tonight. There's a cliff path off the back of that hall.” He grips your shoulder once, hard, and leaves before either of you can do anything worse.`)))+P(`Auntie Tang feeds you at the end of the kitchen shift like it's any other day, then catches your wrist as you stand, and presses something into your palm: a charm hammered from pot-iron, the character for <i>soup</i> on one face and nothing on the other. “For where you're going,” she says. ${G.f.a1_tang_owes?"Then she turns to the whole basement and ladles you out of the white pot in front of everyone, a public benediction, the basement's highest honor conferred at full volume. ":""}You will think about the blank face of that charm for years: the basement's whole theology in one image — soup on one side, and on the other, whatever you can carry.`)+((G.f.yanRespect)?(P(`Yan Shuo falls into step beside you for exactly ten strides on the temple path, eyes forward. “Kang's guards drink at the rite,” he says, conversational, as if remarking on the weather. “I have arranged for their wine to be excellent.” Five more strides. “The frozen stream taught me what your word is worth, weaver. Tonight you'll learn what mine is.” ${G.f.a1_spotted?"At the tenth stride, almost smiling: “I watched you for a month before you caught me. I have never once stopped.” ":""}Fist to palm, and he is gone into the lantern crowd.`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Dusk gathers. The first lanterns go up the steps like sparks up a flue.`,go:"a2c10_river"}]};

SC["a2c10_river"]={img:"rite",
 t:()=>P(`You stand at the wood-yard wall one last time and watch the rite become what it is: ten thousand lights climbing the thousand steps in one unbroken line, the mountain wearing a river of fire on its spine, the cloud-ring at the peak lit from beneath like the lid of a forge.`)+((G.f.a1_intent=="home")?(P(`And for one held breath you see it as a road — every lantern a porch light, every porch light a door someone is keeping open, the whole burning line of them pointing up into the dark the way the dead are supposed to walk. Somewhere at the top of a line like this one, there is a door with your name on it. You are done pretending you've stopped counting the steps.`)):(""))+((G.f.a1_intent=="strong")?(P(`And you see it as a ladder — ten thousand rungs of light, and on every rung a soul holding its little fire and wanting up. A year ago you stood at the bottom carrying water. Tonight your name was read into the rolls over their heads. The wanting in you has stopped being hunger and become architecture: you will climb until the rungs run out, and then you will build.`)):(""))+((G.f.a1_intent=="even")?(P(`And you see it as a ledger — ten thousand entries of light, each lantern a household, each household carrying debts the bearers didn't write, the whole shining column of it climbing to be counted by someone who has never once counted it fairly. Tonight, for one night, a servant's name sits in that ledger's credit column. It is a start. It is nowhere near a balance.`)):(""))+((G.f.a1_intent=="safe")?(P(`And you see it, with the cold clarity that has kept you alive twice now, as a current — ten thousand lights moving one direction, and the only soul on the mountain summoned to swim against it. Every instinct you've sharpened for a year says the same thing the river said the night you died: <i>get out of the water.</i> You stay at the wall until the cold runs out of arguments. There's no version of tonight where you don't walk in.`)):(""))+P(`Granny Sho is sweeping the empty wood-yard behind you, against all custom, on the night the whole mountain climbs. Tap, goes the cane. “The Hall of Quiet Ash hums on rite nights, boy. Every rite night for forty years. The only nights it hums.” The broom stops. ${G.sho>=3?"“Her name was Wen Suyin.” It comes out of the old woman like a splinter coming out of forty-year-old flesh, the first time the name has crossed her lips since the mountain ate it. “My sworn sister. Wen. Su. Yin. If the hall hums tonight — tell it her name back.”":"“My sworn sister went up on a rite night. I have swept the bottom of these steps ever since.” The broom starts again. “Mind which doors hum, boy.”"}`)+P(`A steward materializes at the wood-yard gate, lantern-light on a face that wants to be anywhere else: “Elder Kang summons the new disciple. Hall of Quiet Ash. Now.”`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Walk to the hall through the rising river of light.`,go:"c4_prep"}]};

SC["c4_prep"]={t:()=>P(`The Hall of Quiet Ash sits apart from the sect, old and windowless, a held breath in stone, and the night arranges itself around you at its threshold — every kindness you have planted, come back as harvest:`)+((G.sho>=2)?(P(`Granny Sho steps out of the dark beside the door, cane silent for once. “The hall ate my sister, boy. I have waited forty years at the bottom of these steps.” She presses her old loom shuttle into your hand — it thrums with decades of stored thread — and grips your wrist: “One last lesson. Every technique is a weave, and every weave can be <i>unpicked</i>. Like so.” Knowledge pours through her fingers like cold water.`)):(""))+((G.mei>=3)?(P(`Mei is waiting in the shadow of the gate, pale and furious that you'd go alone, the vial she gave you this morning already counted among your assets and her presence the asset she didn't announce. She does not leave.`)):(""))+((G.bao>=2)?(P(`And off the back of the hall, where the cliff path drops toward the firewood stations, a coil of good hauling rope is tied where no rope should be — knotted, you notice, in the exact clumsy double-hitch you taught a laughing boy behind a woodshed a lifetime ago.`)):(""))+((G.sho<2&&G.mei<3&&G.bao<2)?(P(`You walk to the hall alone. The lanterns climb the mountain behind you like a river of stars, and not one of them is yours.`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Enter the Hall of Quiet Ash.`,do:()=>{if(G.sho>=2){learn("unravel","Unravel");G.maxthr+=2;G.thr=G.maxthr;note("Granny Sho's shuttle: +2 max Threads");}if(G.mei>=3){G.f.elixir=true;note("Cloudpith Elixir: survive one fall");};},go:"c4_reveal"}]};